- How would you implement automated canary testing for failover scenarios?
- What monitoring and observability patterns would you deploy to detect ordering violations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a stateful, TTL-based enrichment with side-input updates, late-data handling, and idempotent sinks in KCNA. Reflects real-world needs for per-user enrichment at scale.

## Key Concepts
- TTL-based in-memory caches for streaming enrichment
- Side-input stream for cache population
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics in sinks
- Re-enrichment triggers and idempotent downstream writes
- Offset management across multi-topic joins

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton enrichment logic
class Enricher {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.cache = new TTLCache(ttlMs); // maps userId -> segment
  }
  enrichMessage(clickEvent) {
    const seg = this.cache.get(clickEvent.userId);
    if (seg) return { ...clickEvent, segment: seg };
    // emit with unknown and schedule re-enrichment on cache update
    return { ...clickEvent, segment: 'unknown' };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test eviction and re-enrichment without data loss?
- How would you scale the TTL cache across multiple workers?
- How would you detect and recover from cache corruption or delays in side-inputs?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of per-tenant security, ACLs, and token lifecycles in KCNA. Assesses gateway/broker enforcement, rotation and revocation strategies, and robust auditing under multi-tenant pressure. Calls for practical test plans and rollback considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant ACLs with topic-level granularity
- JWT/OAuth tokens and short-lived credentials
- Gateway and broker ACL enforcement and performance impact
- Rotation, revocation, and audit logging
- Observability and test strategies with edge cases

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation snippet: token + ACL check
function authorize(token, topic, operation) {
  const claims = decodeJWT(token);
  if (Date.now() >= claims.exp) return false;
  if (!claims.tenants.includes(claims.tenant)) return false;
  const acl = ACL_STORE[claims.tenant]?.[topic];
  if (!acl) return false;
  return acl.includes(operation);
}
```

